cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or these results, please cite the paper below."
title: "Target Length Rather Than Morphological Weighting Reduces Overthinking in Turkish Chain-of-Thought Distillation"
abstract: >-
  Code and analysis for a study of chain-of-thought distillation into small language
  models for Turkish. Controlled, length-matched ablations show that the reduction in
  token exhaustion is produced by the token length of the training target rather than
  by the morphological criterion used to select which sentences to remove.
